<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis holding at firm levels.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis holding at firm levels.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis levels for rail soymeal were mostly holding around recently-established stronger levels Tuesday in quiet conditions.</p>
<p>Dealers noted soymeal export demand from Japan and Europe was steady but not spectacular. Supplies in central Illinois, however, appear to have tightened significantly, prompting recent strength in the basis.</p>
<p>Competition from cottonseed meal was reported to be adversely affecting soymeal demand in some states in the southeast United States. In the truck market the basis continued to be switched to CBOT March futures from January.</p>
<p>Spot rail soymeal (dollars/ton basis CBOT, 47.5 pct protein):</p>
<p> Chicago		     +12.00  +  H	 - unc</p>
<p> Danville, Ill.	    + 9.00  +  H	 - unc</p>
<p> Decatur, Ill. (nom)     +10.00  +  H	 - unc</p>
